course: dictionary
lesson: 11098
title: Wheeze: breath, sound and trick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wheeze has three meanings, and context tells you which one to use. When you wheeze, you breathe with a whistling or rattling sound in your chest because breathing is hard. «Dust mites can make some people sneeze and wheeze.» Here the sentence is about breathing, so wheeze means breathing with that whistling sound.
explain: A wheeze can also be the sound itself, as in «a wheezy chest», where wheezy describes the chest. Old British talk uses wheeze for a clever trick or plan. If someone says «That was a clever wheeze», they are praising a smart idea, not talking about breath at all.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «In asthma the airways tighten and swell, causing wheeze, cough and breathlessness», the words cough and breathlessness are about breathing, so wheeze must mean the breathing sound too. If your meaning makes no sense, try another one.
fact: To wheeze means to breathe with a whistling or rattling sound in the chest.
fact: «Wheeze» can also be a noun, meaning the sound itself, as in «a wheeze».
fact: In asthma, the airways in the lungs can tighten and swell, which can cause a wheeze, a cough and breathlessness.
fact: «Wheeze» can mean a clever trick or plan in old British talk.
fact: If you wheeze and have an inhaler, use it and tell an adult straight away.
exercise: «Dust mites can make some people sneeze and wheeze.» What does wheeze mean here? | To run very fast | *To breathe with a whistling or rattling sound | To laugh loudly until you cry | To fall asleep suddenly
exercise: Grandad says, «That was a clever wheeze to get the best seat first.» What does wheeze mean? | A cough that won't stop | A whistling sound in the chest | *A clever trick or plan | A soft, sleepy noise
exercise: «In asthma the airways tighten and swell, causing wheeze, cough and breathlessness.» Find and copy the word that names a sound made when breathing is hard. | *wheeze | swell | asthma | airways
test: «A stethoscope lets the doctor hear the heart and lungs, and wheezes or crackles can be signs of illness.» What are wheezes in this sentence? | *Sounds that can be signs of illness | Parts of the heart | Tiny spiders with eight legs | Kinds of doctor
test: Maya starts to wheeze during playtime. What should she do? | Hide her inhaler in her bag | Ignore it and keep running hard | *Stop, sit down and tell an adult | Run faster to warm up
exam: In «a wheezy chest», what kind of word is wheezy? | *An adjective | A noun | A verb | An adverb
